{
  "schema_version": "turn.v1",
  "note": "The traces amul-oan-api sends beside its turns, as turn.v1 (amul-telemetry telemetry/turn.v1.yaml): by kind, then by job or event, the trace fields, the amul.* metadata keys and the scores of each. Each root is named after its kind and has no input or output; what the job or the frontend sent is on the observation under it. No turn caused a background job here, so the farmer refresh carries no session or pipeline (its queue is shared by chat and voice). heat_alert_call is one attempt to ring a farmer for a collar heat alert: placed, skipped or error (amul.call_result) and why (amul.call_reason, as the webhook row's call_error says it); a placed call's session is the provider's call id, the session its turns carry. A frontend event is the web app's; only the anonymous token carries a user id. Suggestions are not listed: they are the turn's suggestions step (chat.json).",
  "background_job": {
    "farmer_background_refresh": {
      "trace_fields": [],
      "metadata_keys": [
        "amul.farmer_id",
        "amul.job",
        "amul.kind",
        "amul.release",
        "amul.schema_version",
        "amul.service"
      ],
      "scores": []
    },
    "health_check": {
      "trace_fields": [],
